# Backend Conventions

## Structure

- Entry: `backend/index.js` — mounts routes under `/api/*`
- Routes: one file per domain in `backend/routes/`
- DB pool: `backend/db/index.js` (Neon via `DATABASE_URL`)
- Utils: `backend/utils/s3Storage.js` (R2), `backend/utils/safetyFilter.js` (moderation)

## SQL

- Raw parameterized queries — no ORM
- Schema lives in `backend/schema.sql` (when present)
- Key tables: `users`, `neighborhood_roster`, `announcements`, `community_alerts`, `watercooler_posts`, `community_requests`, `resident_dues`, `ledger_transactions`, `documents`, `verified_vendors`, `neighborhood_events`, `invitations`

## Auth gaps (do not assume middleware exists)

- Login compares password against `password_hash` — bcrypt pending
- Routes trust client-supplied `author_name`, `uploaded_by`, etc.
- Admin endpoints (e.g. `/api/requests/admin/all`) have no server-side auth

## Optional services

Stripe, Sightengine, and OpenAI degrade gracefully when env vars are missing.
